# Product Usage Summary

## Product Used

Oracle Kubernetes Engine on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure

## Purpose

I created this repository after being accepted into the Oracle ACE Apprentice Program to document my product usage and understanding of a basic OKE web application deployment pattern.

## What I Created

I created a simple Kubernetes deployment structure using:

- Deployment
- Service
- Ingress
- Basic NGINX container image
- Architecture flow documentation

## What I Practiced

I reviewed how a containerized web application can be deployed on Oracle Kubernetes Engine and exposed through Kubernetes ingress and OCI load balancing.

## What I Understood

My main understanding is that an OKE deployment has multiple layers. The pod runs the application, the service provides internal routing, the ingress defines the external rule, and the OCI Load Balancer supports access from outside the cluster.

